cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Overbudget Haar-Purity Subsystem Designs Beyond the Quadratic Threshold"
message: "If you use this manuscript or exact-arithmetic verification suite, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Missiaen
    given-names: Thijs
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-3678-0810"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Bruges, Belgium"
    email: "thijs.missiaen@gmail.com"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/thijsmissiaen/haar-purity-overbudget-designs"
abstract: >-
  For an even number n = 2k of d-dimensional quantum subsystems, this work
  resolves the extremal geometry of the complex-Haar subsystem-purity variance
  in the overbudget regime m > n across arbitrary cut budgets 1 <= m <= M_n
  and all integer local dimensions d >= 2 via the harmonic analysis of the
  folded Johnson association scheme J_bar(2k, k).
keywords:
  - Haar-random states
  - subsystem purity
  - folded Johnson scheme
  - Delsarte linear programming
  - Witt Steiner system S(5,6,12)
  - supersaturated designs
  - exact arithmetic verification
